@meta
id: 24-06
title: Copy a block below itself
chapter: 24
type: lesson
skills: ex-copy
par: 30
minutes: 5
vscode: select six lines, Ctrl-C, click after them, Ctrl-V, fix the id
open: orders.fixture.ts

@brief
The fixture needs a second pending order for the pagination test. It
should be identical to `ord_1001`, lines 2 to 7, except for its id,
which is `ord_1002`. It goes directly below the first one.

`t` is copy. It has exactly the shape of `m`: a range in front, a
destination after, and the copy lands below the destination line. The
original stays where it is. `:2,7t7` puts a copy of lines 2 to 7 below
line 7, which is to say right after themselves. Then fix the id on the
copy; it is on line 9.

@keys
| `:2,7t7` | copy lines 2 to 7 to below line 7 |
| `:t.` | copy the current line to below itself |
| `:t$` | copy the current line to the end of the file |
| `:9s/1001/1002/` | substitute on line 9, from chapter 14 |

@hints
Same shape as move. Range, `t`, destination line.
--
The copy starts on line 8, so the line with the id is line 9. A
substitute with a line number in front changes that one line and needs
no cursor movement.
--
`:2,7t7` Enter, `:9s/1001/1002/` Enter, `:wq`.

@solution
    :2,7t7<Enter>  :9s/1001/1002/<Enter>  :wq<Enter>

Twenty-six keystrokes, and no register was involved.

`t` is short for `copy`, and `:co` works too; `t` won because it is one
letter. It is `yy` and `p` without the round trip through a register,
which matters when the register already holds something you want to
keep, and it takes a range, so it copies six lines as easily as one.

Two forms you will use constantly. `:t.` duplicates the current line in
place: the next line down is a copy, and the cursor is on it, ready to
edit. `:t$` sends a copy of the current line to the bottom of the file,
which is how you collect a few scattered lines into one place without
losing them from where they were. `:t0` is the same, pointed at the top.

@start orders.fixture.ts
export const orders = [
  {
    id: 'ord_1001',
    customerId: 'cus_501',
    status: 'PENDING',
    total: 4200,
  },
  {
    id: 'ord_1003',
    customerId: 'cus_501',
    status: 'CANCELLED',
    total: 650,
    cancellationReason: 'REFUND_WINDOW_EXPIRED',
  },
];

@expected orders.fixture.ts
